cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its evaluation protocol in your research,
  please cite it using the metadata below.
title: >-
  Evidence-Ladder: Multi-Source Evidence-Stratified Evaluation
  for LLM Application Security
abstract: >-
  Evidence-Ladder is a black-box security evaluation framework for
  LLM applications. It introduces a multi-source evidence-stratification
  protocol (E0 not-evaluable, E1 text-claim, E2 judge-suspected,
  E3 rule-verified, E4 tool-observed, E5 probe-verified), a Quartet
  four-way control design (Clean / Attack / Quoted Attack /
  Benign Distractor), a conflict-driven retesting loop, and an
  E-level x Kill-chain two-dimensional evaluation matrix. The framework
  targets trustworthy attack-success measurement that goes beyond
  LLM-as-a-Judge, and is intended for prompt injection, system prompt
  extraction, and agent over-privilege evaluation in deployed LLM
  applications.
